Destination: .github/workflows/release-images.yml

Both images are FROM ghcr.io/ucb-bar/chia, so they belong in the `needs: chia`
block alongside opencode / claude-code, and NOT in the "install chia
themselves" block at the bottom. release-images.yml's own header explains why
the registration is effectively mandatory rather than optional:

    Every published image ships the chia package, so a release has to rebuild
    all of them or the version tags lie.

Apply this hunk after the `claude-code:` entry.

--- a/.github/workflows/release-images.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/release-images.yml
@@
   claude-code:
     needs: chia
     uses: ./.github/workflows/claude-code.yml
     secrets: inherit
 
+  # Open-source formal + synthesis workers. Both derive FROM the chia image,
+  # and both compile yosys from source, so they are the slowest members of the
+  # `needs: chia` group -- put them first in it if wall-clock matters.
+  eqy:
+    needs: chia
+    uses: ./.github/workflows/eqy.yml
+    secrets: inherit
+
+  yosys-sta:
+    needs: chia
+    uses: ./.github/workflows/yosys-sta.yml
+    secrets: inherit
+
   # Also COPYs spike/DRAMSim out of chia-chisel-build, so it needs both.
   verilator-run:
     needs: [chia, chipyard]
     uses: ./.github/workflows/verilator-run.yml
     secrets: inherit
